WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:04.440
My own token, against
the entitlements API.

2
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:08.350
401. One command later, the same call:

3
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:12.200
200. Nothing changed in the token.

4
00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.320
Something changed in who
the stack thinks I am.

5
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:25.100
Service path. Who is asking.

6
00:00:26.206 --> 00:00:28.776
Who does the stack think you are?

7
00:00:30.184 --> 00:00:34.514
spi token --me prints
your own Azure token.

8
00:00:34.744 --> 00:00:37.634
Your call comes in through
the stack's one gateway.

9
00:00:37.864 --> 00:00:42.744
The mesh accepts the token's issuer, and
the sidecar in front of each service writes

10
00:00:42.744 --> 00:00:45.074
your unique_name as the caller.

11
00:00:45.384 --> 00:00:49.074
Then entitlements looks you up,
and finds no groups for you.

12
00:00:49.544 --> 00:00:54.594
So you get 401. Plain spi
token calls as the platform,

13
00:00:54.744 --> 00:00:57.634
not as you, which is why it always worked.

14
00:00:59.884 --> 00:01:05.884
spi users add --me reads
your token and stores

15
00:01:05.884 --> 00:01:08.054
the id the mesh will write for you.

16
00:01:08.284 --> 00:01:12.534
The platform writes your groups, and
the command checks with your own token,

17
00:01:12.604 --> 00:01:14.294
for up to a minute.

18
00:01:14.364 --> 00:01:19.174
Here, it answered, and the
same curl returned 200.

19
00:01:21.626 --> 00:01:25.876
A role is a preset of groups,
and you hold one at a time.

20
00:01:26.346 --> 00:01:29.716
Viewer is users and datalake viewers.

21
00:01:30.266 --> 00:01:34.106
Editor, admin and ops each
add their own groups,

22
00:01:34.106 --> 00:01:35.476
and impersonation.

23
00:01:36.026 --> 00:01:39.316
Editor and above also
let ingestion run as you,

24
00:01:39.546 --> 00:01:40.916
which comes next.

25
00:01:43.278 --> 00:01:44.518
An easy mistake:

26
00:01:44.518 --> 00:01:49.408
running spi users add again
adds to the role I hold.

27
00:01:49.558 --> 00:01:53.088
It replaces it. Here,
viewer became editor.

28
00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:56.608
Users stayed. Editors and
impersonation were added,

29
00:01:56.678 --> 00:01:59.008
and datalake viewers was removed.

30
00:01:59.078 --> 00:02:02.048
Going back to viewer
removes impersonation too.

31
00:02:02.198 --> 00:02:04.608
Check with spi users list.

32
00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:08.356
So now you can say:

33
00:02:08.506 --> 00:02:12.196
the mesh lets my token
in, entitlements decides,

34
00:02:12.266 --> 00:02:15.156
and my role is the one preset I last set.

35
00:02:17.442 --> 00:02:21.692
Next: what does a new environment
hold, and does ingestion work?

